{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 and Mathlib proof that there is an 8-regular simple graph of girth 7 on 768 vertices (Mathlib's SimpleGraph, IsRegularOfDegree and girth), so that the order n(8, 7) of an (8, 7)-cage is at most 768; the House of Graphs cage table listed 774 when this was written. The graph is data (adjacency lists in a binary trie). Lean's kernel checks (decide +kernel, no native_decide) that it is simple and 8-regular, and, for every vertex v and every two neighbours x ≠ y, that the ends of the non-backtracking walks of length at most 3 starting with the edge v x are disjoint from those starting with v y. A cycle of length at most 6 would contradict this at one of its vertices, and an explicit 7-cycle gives girth exactly 7.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Arhan Canli"
    }
  ],
